From: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: retain UserPD boot ownership on shutdown failure

The remoteproc core retains its power reference when shutdown fails.
Only clear the WLAN ownership flag and group accounting after a
successful rproc_shutdown(), allowing subsequent recovery.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -352,11 +352,19 @@
 {
 	struct ath12k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab);
 
+	int ret;
+
 	if (!ab_ahb->userpd_booted)
 		return;
 
+	ret = rproc_shutdown(ab_ahb->tgt_rproc);
+	if (ret) {
+		ath12k_err(ab, "failed to shut down UserPD%u remoteproc: %d\n",
+			   ab_ahb->userpd_id, ret);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	ab_ahb->userpd_booted = false;
-	rproc_shutdown(ab_ahb->tgt_rproc);
 	ab->ag->num_userpd_started--;
 }
 
